  "notes": "The passenger scheme (ETH/standard) plus a 'Cargo' title, with the titles lower on the windowless freighter. Measured on the 777F ET-AVT (left, 2026-10-01); ET-BAA (right, 2025-05-25) agrees. The 767-300F ET-BBF wears it too, with 'Cargo' under '-opian'. Temporary 'Pharma Wing' engine titles (ET-AVT) and '80 years' decals not drawn. Freighters have no cabin windows. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on ET-AVT (777F, left, 2026-10-01, a little from ahead): lengths measured, Ethiopian 0.29 (x ~0.135-0.43), Cargo 0.103, the Amharic 0.076, the small Ethiopia 0.025; the serif lowercase stands 0.62 of the capitals. ET-AVT also carries a small 'Land of Origins' under 'Ethiopia' and 'Pharma Wing' on the engines (not drawn). The photo is foreshortened toward the tail, so the aft titles' places were left as drawn. The fin's three bands are curved sweeps (smooth).",
  "history": "New file. Ethiopian's freighters have worn the 2010 passenger scheme with 'Cargo' added since it was introduced."
}
